<title>USA: Northwest Airlines, union to start talks.</title>
<headline>Northwest Airlines, union to start talks.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Negotiations between Northwest Airlines Corp and Teamsters Local 2000, which represents flight attendants, are scheduled to begin Wednesday, the union said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The current contract expired August 1, Teamsters said.</p>
<p>A survey of more than 6,000 flight attendants indicated the most important issues in the negotiations were compensation, retirement and scheduling flexibility, Teamsters said.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312 408-8787</p>
